  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Proportion of total government spending on essential services (education, health and social protection)

Mapping of gaps from unfunded mandates and costs at the local level

Formulation of policies, especially fiscal, wage and social protection policies, that progressively achieve greater equality

Capacities in high-level decision making on SDG budgeting improved</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2020">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">50% (including culture)

N/a

No SDG financing mechanism in place

N/a</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Analysis of SDG-related budgetary spending during 2015-2019 completed

Screening legislation on funding of mandates at the local level and EU acquis compliance assessment completed

Drafting process of SDG financing strategy / INFF started

Capacity development activities with the Parliamentary Sub-committee on Sustainable Development designed and delivered</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Analysis of SDG-related budgetary spending during 2015-2019 completed

Call for expertise for screening legislation on funding of mandates at the local level and EU acquis compliance assessment launched

Scoping for INFF started. Preliminary roadmap drafted. Recruitment for INFF in process. 

The general elections of April 2021 brought changes to the composition of the Parliament. The Parliamentary Sub-committee on Sustainable Development was not reconvened. Discussions on identification of needs are re-established with the Parliamentary Committee on Economy and Finance.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conducting the analysis of SDG-related budgetary spending during 2015-2019 

Screening legislation on funding of mandates at the local level and EU acquis compliance assessment

Preparatory work for drafting the SDG financing strategy started

Members of the Parliamentary Sub-committee on Sustainable Development supported on mainstreaming SDGs in the national policy</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Analysis of SDG-related budgetary spending during 2015-2019 in progress

Screening of legislation on funding of mandates at the local level and EU acquis compliance assessment expected in 2021

Preparatory work for drafting the SDG financing strategy / INFF set to begin after the finalization of the SDG-related budgetary spending analysis

Discussions with the Parliamentary Sub-committee on Sustainable Development on capacity building needs in progress</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">52%

Legislation screening on funding of mandates at the local level finalized. Findings contributing to broader policy dialogue on the role and financing of local government units for sustainable development and social protection

INFF finalized and adopted

Members of the Parliament, and particularly the Parliamentary Committee on Economy and Finance, supported to monitor the budgetary drafting and monitoring process with an SDG-lens</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
